	(text "VIN input: fuse, reverse-polarity diode, surge clamp and the VIN sense divider"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "905066dc-4eb3-50d5-bd19-dddf534c5f2b")
	)
	(text_box "WHAT IT DOES\nThe vehicle supply (9-30 V DC, 12 V nominal) comes in on J1 pin 9. F101 limits the current, D103 blocks a reversed\nsupply, D104 clamps voltage spikes. The protected supply VIN_LM feeds the 5V buck. D102 + R101 send a small sample of\nthe supply voltage to the ESP32 (VIN_SENSE), so the firmware can measure the battery voltage.\n\nPINS OF THIS MODULE (its block on the top sheet)\nVIN_IN (in): vehicle supply from J1 pin 9 (Vehicle net class: 0.8 mm clearance)\nVIN_LM (out): protected supply to the 5V buck (U101 VIN, C102, C103)\nVIN_SENSE (out): to ESP32 GPIO36; R102 (5.6k to GND) and C101 (100 nF) finish the divider in the ESP32 + USB module\nGND: ground (battery negative, J1 pins 1 and 2)\nPower and ground reach the parts on this sheet only through these pins: the ground and supply symbols drawn on this sheet are local to it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 17.78 0)
		(size 265 26.55)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d964f5ae-5b89-5381-bb21-18862a782801")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 137.16 91.44)
		(end 160.02 116.84)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type dash)
			(color 200 60 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "d25f1cdf-8cf6-50c4-9ca0-ee64065c001f")
	)
	(text "D104 at the buck input"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 137.76 92.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c6c33281-d451-53a1-aac6-8f74d3054b31")
	)
	(text "D104 clamps surges: give it a short, wide path to GND\n(a via or two right at its GND pad) and keep it near\nthe 5V buck input (C102/C103, U101 pin 1).\nVIN chain tracks: 1.0 mm wide where they fit."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 106.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ddc8632b-683a-5a9c-a0ce-80cffa9e998c")
	)
	(text_box "PARTS AND THEIR JOBS\nF101: 0.5 A resettable fuse (60 V): opens when too much current flows (a short on the board) and resets itself once it cools.\nD103: SS54 Schottky diode (40 V, 5 A): reverse-polarity protection. If VIN and GND are swapped it blocks, so nothing behind it sees a negative voltage.\nD104: SMAJ30CA TVS diode: clamps voltage spikes on VIN_LM (load dump, ISO 7637 pulses); it starts to conduct at about 33 V. The board takes 32 V steady at most.\nD102: 1N4148W small diode: lets only positive voltage into the sense divider, so GPIO36 never sees a reversed supply.\nR101: 100k: top resistor of the VIN sense divider. With R102 (5.6k) VIN_SENSE is about (VIN - 0.5 V) x 0.053: 0.6 V at 12 V, 1.6 V at 30 V.\nVIN_RAW: Net label: the supply after the fuse, before the reverse-polarity diode."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 156 0)
		(size 155 22.45)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "35700246-ad3f-5cf0-a3fe-134536d09ad6")
	)
